@@ -4,4 +4,24 @@ Consumes `price.changed` events and pushes prices to the marketplace partner's p
 Only brands that are eligible for the website are sent; the eligible list comes from the
 nightly warehouse export `eligible_brands.csv` (see `warehouse-sql/procs/eligible_brands.sql`).
 
+## Admin endpoints
+
+Served on `ADMIN_PORT` (8081), fronted by the `price-sync-admin` service.
+
+- `GET /healthz`
+- `POST /admin/reload-eligible-brands` — re-reads `eligible_brands.csv` so brand changes
+  take effect without restarting the service. Responds `{"status": "reloaded",
+  "eligible_brands": <count>}`, or 500 if the export can't be read, in which case the
+  previously loaded list stays in effect.
+
+Two things to know before relying on it:
+
+- It reloads the **export file**, not the warehouse. A `web_eligible` change made by
+  merchandising only reaches the file when `export_eligible_brands()` next runs (nightly,
+  02:00 UTC — see `deploy-config/jobs/schedules.yaml`), so re-run that export first,
+  then call this endpoint.
+- It reloads **one replica**. prod runs 4, and the admin service load-balances across them,
+  so a single call leaves the others on the old list. Call it until every replica reports
+  the expected `eligible_brands` count, or restart the deployment instead.
+
 Run tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`
